  "notes": "Reusable checked linear operator for inference only; Kokoro ALBERT projection is one consumer. FP64 accumulation is deliberately distinct from PyTorch's FP32 reduction and uses an explicit numerical tolerance. Pinned first Kokoro ALBERT FFN projection at [36,2048] to [36,768] differs from PyTorch 2.8 FP32 by 3.814697265625e-5 on oracle-fed inputs while matching independently executed FP64 arithmetic exactly. Its new composition fixture declares its own 5e-5 absolute projection/residual bound and keeps normalized outputs at 1e-5; existing projection/QKV bounds remain unchanged. Direct pinned full-model SDPA hooks show that the first Q/K/V projections already differ in the connected graph before attention reduction; pinned PyTorch 2.8 same-input replay attributes up to 2.38e-6, 2.86e-6 and 1.55e-6, respectively, to this provider's local reduction contract. These observations do not identify a universally preferable reduction order. If a tighter PyTorch-dispatch match is required, add a separately named reduction provider/contract rather than modifying this FP64 provider.",
